Restore the signed WORD rectangle fields used by the three statistics viewers.

The original callers of Draw_Semi_Trans_Poly read adjacent DWORDs and SAR 16:
Championship @0x44ce34/0x44ce3d, Driver @0x44d04d/0x44d056 (see caller
disassembly), and Track in View_Track_Stats. Their Y/width fields are signed
16-bit values, matching the rectangle descriptors and short arguments.
The decompiler's fallback BYTE aliases discarded negative Y coordinates and
the Championship width's high byte. The resulting table backgrounds were
drawn outside the visible slab, although all statistics text was correct.

Use the actual descriptor WORDs: Championship (-42,282), Driver (-28,132),
Track (-38,218). The existing X and height loads already preserve their WORDs.
The persisted-statistics UI comparison exercises all three actual viewers
with an original-generated completed season and compares full 64-phase frames.

